'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 10''' was the tenth weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on October 14, 2026 at the Aizawa Municipal Gymnasium in [[Aizawa, Aizawa|Aizawa]], [[Aizawa Prefecture]]. The show was the first [[NOPW Wednesday]] since Episode 9 on August 19, following the promotion's two-month pause of the weekly series for the [[G1 Climax 2026]] tour, and served as the go-home show for the [[G1 Climax 2026 Final]] at the [[Aizawa Dome]] four days later.

== Background ==

The G1 Climax 2026 block stage ended on October 10 in [[Toyozawa]], when [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]] defeated [[Takagi Yuto]] in the first playoff match in G1 history to win Block B. The Final was set: [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] — the Intercontinental Champion, winner of Block A with the first perfect block in G1 history at 8-0-1 — against Taumafa, with the winner challenging [[Leoni Masua]] for the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] at [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]] on January 4.

Vance held to the silence that had defined his entire tournament: no interviews, no media, no appearances. Taumafa and the Vaiahi family carried the promotion week alone. NOPW announced a [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]] contract signing for Episode 10 — the champion at the table, and an empty chair for the G1 winner.

