== Match details ==

* '''Match 1:''' G1 rematch — Ono had beaten Tanaka in Naruto during the block stage, and the Bulldog wanted it back. Tanaka's brawling took the young ace to the floor twice, but the Ono Driver at 11:12 ended it clean. '''Crowd:''' '''ONO''' chants throughout. POP for the finish.
* '''Match 2:''' The CHAOS juniors built momentum for their [[IGO Junior Tag Team Championship]] match at the Final — Sato pinning Yamamoto after the Prince's Landing at 12:38. Iwata and Yamamoto took the champions' challengers to the limit. '''Crowd:''' split building, dueling chants.
* '''Match 3:''' The number reclaimed. Ishida — whose G1 began with an 8:56 humiliation against Jusuf Muntasir in Okami — submitted El Phantasma with the Ishida Lock in exactly 8:56. The building understood immediately. '''Crowd:''' ERUPTION at the time announcement. '''ISHIDA''' chants. Standing ovation.
* '''Match 4:''' Another G1 rematch — Maeda had beaten Nakamura in Aizawa during Round 2. The Flash evened it with the Flash Flood at 15:47, four days before he and El Phantasma defend the junior tag titles at the Dome. Maeda, who challenges [[Koji Endo]] for the [[IGO Junior Heavyweight Championship]] at the Final, took the loss clean. '''Crowd:''' '''SPEED STAR''' chants. HEAT for the Flash's celebration.
* '''Match 5:''' The go-home statement. Taumafa ran through the Cannon Club's wall — the hip attack, the corner splash, and the Samoan driver at 9:33. Diallo, the man Kengo hides behind, never got started. '''Crowd:''' '''TAUMAFA''' chants. The family's diaspora section on its feet for the entrance and the finish.
* '''Match 6:''' The semi-main — KAZUKI's tune-up for [[Daigo Kuroki]] at the Final, against Honda's Asikyran traditional wrestling. Honda's mat game held the former champion for thirteen minutes before the Twin Star Press at 13:20. KAZUKI bowed to Honda after the bell — the respect of the block stage. '''Crowd:''' '''KAZUKI''' chants. Respect applause for Honda.

== Main event segment: The Wrestling Summit contract signing ==

The show closed with the contract signing for the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] match at [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]]. [[Leoni Masua]] sat at the table with the championship and the namo. Beside him, an empty chair — for the winner of the G1 Final.

Taumafa came out alone, spoke for both finalists: ''"Sunday, the family finishes what it started. And whoever stands across from the chief in Toyozawa — the table will still have a head."''

Leoni signed, then looked at the empty chair and spoke for the first time in the build: ''"I don't care which of you wins. I've beaten the giant. I've never beaten the silence. Come and show me."''

[[Marcus Vance]] did not appear. The silence held to the end of the broadcast.

'''Crowd:''' '''LEONI''' chants. MEGA POP for the line. Loud '''VANCE''' chants for the man who was not there.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The silence holds.''' Vance's absence from the go-home show was itself the story — four days from the biggest match of his career, the Workhorse said nothing, showed nothing, and let the empty chair speak.
* '''8:56, reclaimed.''' Ishida's submission of El Phantasma at exactly 8:56 turned the number of his humiliation into his own. The television champion enters his Final defense against [[Honda Masanori]] with seven submissions since the G1 began.
* '''The family carries the week.''' With Vance silent, Taumafa did every interview, every appearance, and the go-home statement — a 9:33 demolition of the Cannon Club's wall.
* '''Junior title picture.''' Sato & Kimura and Nakamura both won going into the junior tag title match at the Final; Maeda's loss does nothing to cool his shot at Endo.

